{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1312905-why-the-change-in-kinain-becoming-dreamstuck-will-there-be-an-enchanted-book","id":1312905,"title":"Why the change in Kinain? Becoming Dreamstuck? Will there be an Enchanted book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-18T00:24:47-07:00","id":1312905,"title":"Why the change in Kinain? Becoming Dreamstuck? Will there be an Enchanted book?","content":"I admit, I finally have gotten around to reading C20, and while there are updates I love, there are a few things that upset the long-time player in me. One of those is.... Kinain and Enchanted.<br /> <br /> I saw nothing about Enchanted mortals becoming Dreamstruck -- maybe they replaced it with Bedlam or its equivalent elsewhere in the book, but I guess I loved the flavor-text of the Enchanted book. They'd given examples of the addictive quality of Glamour, and a HUGE part of the personal-tragedy angle that kept Fae as outsiders was the distance from mortals they had to keep, for their own protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> But unless I am missing something, C20 took the tragedy away from being Fae and having Kinain children, or being a Kinain with Fae parents. The bittersweetness of being a Fae parent enjoying the wonder of a Kinain child while young, yet knowing it was a fleeting thing. Like a selkie tale in reverse, it was the common experiences of all Fae parents watching their Kinain child grow up, grow apart, eventually forgetting the Dreaming to go off to the mortal world, where they 'belong'.<br /> <br /> <br /> But even so, out in the world, kinain didn't quite fit in with ordinary mortals, either, because they were too 'fey'.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was wonderful and terrible, it made the children of Fae sort of tragic figures. Caught between worlds, and unable to fit in with either -- yet if they stayed in the Dreaming too long, or a Fae parent tried to keep a Kinain child close, they would eventually go mad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh, I can see everything and don't forget anything, my parents and I have this cool bond, and I can even do cantrips! My bestie is the Duke's daughter and everybody's cool with it. I even have a pet chimera and run errands for the Court.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> You see what I mean? It lacks the wrenching choices to be made, the balancing act between wanting to share what you are with the potential danger to the mortals you love when you Enchant them. How they will react, what they might do to keep the Dreaming and their memories of it close?<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the aspects emphasized in playing Kinain, was how vulnerable Kinain were to unscrupulous Fae, how bereft they felt when they fell to the Mists and knew something was missing -- and how some could so easily be blackmailed into servitude in return for Glamour <i>(part of which went away when the writers decided they can just make their own?)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I think C20 went a little too far towards making them the equivalent of Shifter Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <br /> Am I wrong, did I miss something? Will there be other books out there to clarify later? Or is the personal-tragedy aspect of Kinain and Enchanted mortals getting tossed out the window? Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","user":"Observer","date":". 05-18-2019, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","name":"Observer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T21:05:58-07:00","id":1313062,"title":"","content":"I think that the changes you mentioned may have been made to try and take away certain elements involving being born into a hostile environment. The past version of Kinain,a s you mentioned, naturally became the heart of dramatic situations and trouble by virtue of their birth. However, there's been a lot of change in the world around us since the Kinain were first introduced, and the kind of drama that you mention could rub players the wrong way AND have them voice their displeasure. Enough people have to deal with being attacked based on traits they've had since birth (race, gender, orientation) or other qualities that emerge later but were inborn in some way; bringing that into a game can be aggravating. Not sure if this WAS a factor, but it did come to mind. Changeling was a game that needed a lot of other updates with the setting due to the changes in society since then, and someone may have thought that was one of them.<br /> <br /> Also, you are underplaying the drama that IS there. The focus changes from &quot;Am I going to endanger my child&quot; to &quot;How soon will my child look older than me? Will banality take me before then?&quot; and similar questions. There are examples in there of Kinain being left out as they age and their friends stay young for far longer, Also, they get a front row seat on the world of magic, but can't really get into the world as a player. You're forced to realize that you're a guest, but not really a valued member, of changeling society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T08:47:49-07:00","id":1313129,"title":"","content":"I play a changeling dealing with taking care of an undone fae parent. A friend has kinian character taking care of a undone parent... so there is some of that still. just with the aged instead of the young.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13025-magpie-and-sunshine","name":"Magpie and Sunshine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T18:57:15-07:00","id":1313231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1312905-why-the-change-in-kinain-becoming-dreamstuck-will-there-be-an-enchanted-book?p=1313062#post1313062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the changes you mentioned may have been made to try and take away certain elements involving being born into a hostile environment. The past version of Kinain,a s you mentioned, naturally became the heart of dramatic situations and trouble by virtue of their birth. However, there's been a lot of change in the world around us since the Kinain were first introduced, and the kind of drama that you mention could rub players the wrong way AND have them voice their displeasure. Enough people have to deal with being attacked based on traits they've had since birth (race, gender, orientation) or other qualities that emerge later but were inborn in some way; bringing that into a game can be aggravating. Not sure if this WAS a factor, but it did come to mind. Changeling was a game that needed a lot of other updates with the setting due to the changes in society since then, and someone may have thought that was one of them.<br /> <br /> Also, you are underplaying the drama that IS there. The focus changes from &quot;Am I going to endanger my child&quot; to &quot;How soon will my child look older than me? Will banality take me before then?&quot; and similar questions. There are examples in there of Kinain being left out as they age and their friends stay young for far longer, Also, they get a front row seat on the world of magic, but can't really get into the world as a player. You're forced to realize that you're a guest, but not really a valued member, of changeling society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless the Changelings buy fairy eternity or become siochain there's no real difference in aging....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T22:14:49-07:00","id":1313253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1312905-why-the-change-in-kinain-becoming-dreamstuck-will-there-be-an-enchanted-book?p=1313231#post1313231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unless the Changelings buy fairy eternity or become siochain there's no real difference in aging....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So this may or may not be mentioned in the rest of the book, but the Enchanted appendix (page 457) clearly states that it's less a difference in aging naturally as conditions around them. Time spent in the Dreaming doesn't count evidently (or at least puts aging off and then catches up over a compressed period outside). Kinain can't spend that much time in the dreaming, and thus end up older than any other &quot;kid&quot; changelings they were friends with in childhood, sometimes appearing as much as twice that age. It even mentions that conservative Freeholds often don't want their children mingling with the Kinain of the same age despite them being able to work with them in both worlds, possibly as a result of these problems. The Dreaming Chapter doesn't specify such an effect, but it does mention time can be different in the Dreaming. And, given the Dreaming Purification System in the Far and Deep Dreaming, they may be getting infused with Glamour and purifying Banality, which can affect the aging if the ST allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}